How to correlate the chatloop against llama-cli output

The llama-cli output does not reliably interpret the chat_template.
Therefore we run llama-cli in no-cnv mode, which in turn implies
that we need to provide it with a rendered template.  To do this,
uncomment the code block in the chatloop that creates the rendered
file.  in llm_manager.py look for:

        # enable this file creation for correlation tests (against llama-cli).
        # then run tokenize_my_prompt_with_llama
        # with open("/tmp/test_prompt.txt", "w") as f:
        #     f.write(rendered[len("<|begin_of_text|>"):])

run for long enough to generate the prompt.  Then run
./tokenize_my_prompt_with_llama.sh, which will pick up the
rendered prompt from the previous step.

The .chatconfig.json file in this directory has settings aproppriate
to and matched with the settings in ./tokenize_my_prompt_with_llama.sh.

Note that in prior tests we only matched to a few dozen tokens of
output, but the output kept re-converging and re-diverging.  This is
believed to be due to differences in the library and llama-cli
codebase; the library is a few weeks newer.